inguishes this result from the numerical accident discussed in Section 10.4. Elements are populated by aufbau filling: electrons are added one at a time, and the sequence of ground-state configurations traces a monotone path through the lattice. A set generated by a monotone accumulation of this kind is closed downward by construction. The order-ideal property is the order-theoretic shadow of the filling process. This also explains why the property survives the known irregularities: the lanthanide and actinide anomalies alter which cell is reached at which atomic number but do not remove any cell from the accumulated set, so ordering is disturbed while downward closure is not.')]));

